<title>JAPAN: DDI rises on report of bright earnings.</title>
<headline>DDI rises on report of bright earnings.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>DDI Corp shares rose on Tuesday after a business daily reported that the firm's earnings were likely to exceed previous forecasts, brokers said.</p>
<p>As of 0130 GMT, the shares were up 6,000 yen at 739,000.</p>
<p>The Nihon Keizai Shimbun said DDI's parent current profit was expected to be 67 billion yen in the year to March 31, 1997, larger than the company's November forecast of 60 billion yen.</p>
<p>DDI is one of Japan's long-distance domestic telecommunications operators.</p>
</text>
